+From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
+Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: offload 802.11s to the NSS firmware
+
+On a firmware line that forwards a mesh itself, a mesh interface is
+registered with the NSS firmware as a mesh device and mesh nodes instead
+of as a virtual device. Frames to it stay 802.11, without the QoS control,
+which the hardware inserts. The mesh path table is mirrored to the
+firmware, and its path events go back to mac80211. Multicast the firmware
+receives on the mesh enters mac80211 as 802.11, which forwards it and
+drops duplicates.
+
+The firmware transmits mesh data itself, so the transmit status mac80211
+builds the airtime metric from is taken from the PPDU statistics instead.
+An open mesh installs no key, so a mesh peer is authorised in the firmware
+when the station is.
+
